@startuml llev-compilation
' Compilation pipeline for a `.llev` phonetic-rule file (the LibLevenshtein
' phonetic rule-set DSL). Source text is lexed, parsed into an AST, loaded into a
' ruleset, and lowered to a compiled ruleset; at run time `apply_rules_seq`
' rewrites a token stream into phonetically-normalised tokens. The bundled rules
' cover 53 languages.
' Colour mapping (per the canonical legend):
'   DSL compilation stages  brown  #D7CCC8 (container) / #EFEBE9 (child tint)
'   phonetic-engine output  pink   #F8BBD0
' Arrow colour = DSL border #4E342E for the compile flow.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 14
  BorderColor #455A64
  FontColor #102027
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowThickness 2

left to right direction

title `.llev` phonetic-rule compilation — source → lexer → AST → ruleset → compiled → normalised tokens

rectangle ".llev source" as SRC #D7CCC8
rectangle "lexer\n(src/phonetic/llev/lexer.rs)" as LEX #EFEBE9
rectangle "AST\n(ast.rs)" as AST #EFEBE9
rectangle "loader / ruleset\n(loader.rs, ruleset.rs)" as RULESET #EFEBE9
rectangle "compiled ruleset\n(compiled.rs)" as COMPILED #D7CCC8
rectangle "apply_rules_seq →\nphonetically-normalised tokens" as OUT #F8BBD0

SRC      -[#4E342E]-> LEX
LEX      -[#4E342E]-> AST
AST      -[#4E342E]-> RULESET
RULESET  -[#4E342E]-> COMPILED
COMPILED -[#AD1457]-> OUT

note bottom of RULESET
  Bundled rule-sets cover 53 languages.
end note
@enduml
